Title: The Third Eye (test scene)
Credit: written by
Author: Colby Gutierrez-Kraybill
Draft date: 2026-10-22
Notes: Pipeline test — key frames, in-betweens, sound, Scratch. ~55 s. May never be used.

/* CODUBEE: flat black cat, white eyes. Two eyes until the end of this scene.
   FRIEND is a placeholder: a second cat, not yet designed. It could equally be a
   sibling (see the note at the end); nothing in the action depends on which. */

EXT. BACK GARDEN - MORNING

Sunlight. Tall grass. A moth bobs past.

A tiny black kitten, CODUBEE (two eyes), pounces — misses — tumbles — comes up batting at a dandelion. Picks it up. Blows. The seeds fly.

CODUBEE
(giggling)
Again!

Codubee watches the seeds drift away over the fence...

DISSOLVE TO:

EXT. ALLEY BEHIND THE GARDEN - DUSK

That evening. CODUBEE, still a small kitten, trots along the top of a fence beside FRIEND, an older, bigger cat. They bump. Easy. Close.

FRIEND
Race you to the yard.

They freeze. Below, a DOG creeps out of an opening in a fence, low, stalking them. A GROWL.

The cats leap down and bolt. The dog forces its way through the fence after them, snarling.

Friend springs off Codubee's back — all four legs — pushing the kitten into the dirt, and is gone.

The dog's jaws, inches away. Codubee scrambles, wriggles free, squeezes under a fence board. Barely.

EXT. YARD - A LITTLE LATER

Codubee, ruffled, finds Friend sitting in the yard, licking a paw. Completely unbothered. Friend glances over: careless, satisfied.

CLOSE ON CODUBEE

Their two eyes fill with understanding: Friend put their own safety before Codubee's.

DISSOLVE TO:

CLOSE ON CODUBEE - YEARS LATER

The same face, grown: a lanky teen now. The same look. The lesson has landed: be mindful who your friends are.

On their forehead, a seam of light. A THIRD EYE opens for the first time.

It sees clearly. And it is the only eye that cries.

A single tear runs from the third eye.

Rain begins.

FADE OUT.

/* NOTE (sibling variant): replace FRIEND with a sibling; add one line early in the
   garden scene showing them as kittens together, so the shove reads as family. */
